  "instance_name": "anti_black_stereotype_hyperfocus",
  "label": "Anti-Black Stereotype: Hyperfocus or 'Always Watching'",
  "description": "The meme relies on the stereotype that Black people are hyper-focused, intense, or 'always watching,' which is often used in a derogatory way to imply suspicion, vigilance, or an exaggerated level of attentiveness. This stereotype is reinforced by the image of the Black man intensely focused on the laptop, which is framed as a humorous but racially charged trope.",
